{"v":"3.0.0","project":{"accession":"PRJNA1346419","title":"Developing a novel electrocatalytic anammox process to drive high-efficiency nitrogen removal under ultra-low nitrite conditions in an up-flow electrochemical anaerobic membrane bioreactor","description":"The proposed EAPND system overcomes the conventional anammox reliance on nitrite by achieving 89.7% TN removal with only NH4+-N/NO2--N = 1:0.4 in the influent. Under 2.5 V applied voltage, electrochemical stimulation promoted direct ammonium oxidation by anammox bacteria while enabling electron transfer to cathodic DNB for nitrate reduction to nitrite. Effluent reflux (1:1 ratio) enhanced nitrite reuse, as supported by Random Forest modeling. Microbial analysis revealed dominant enrichment of Candidatus_Brocadia at the anode, with anode-derived protein-like substances stimulating functional genera such as norank_o__Fimbriimonadales(13.8%) and Denitratisoma (5.7%). Notably, the system maintained 60.8% TN removal without nitrite supply, highlighting its electrochemical independence. Compared to PDA and PNA processes, the EAPND system offers superior efficiency and cost-effectiveness by eliminating organic carbon and aeration requirements, providing a novel electrochemical-anammox route for sustainable nitrogen removal.","organism":null,"data_type":"Raw sequence reads","center_name":"East china normal university","submission_date":"2025/10/17 00:00","last_update":null},"sample_cols":["accession","title","collection_date","country","region","city","lat","lon","urban_status","urban_context","eligibility_reason","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","host","location_resolution","country_iso2","place_id","location_status","location_method","location_note","geo_loc_raw","collection_year"],"samples":[["SAMN52833736","Metagenome or environmental sample from sludge metagenome","2024-09-13","China","Shanghai","Shanghai",31.03333,121.45166,"probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","city-leve